From: IdentityV on Mac maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] gdi32: shape valid surrogate pairs in ordinary LTR text

CodeWeavers 26.1 / Wine 11.0 routes ordinary LTR supplementary characters
around BIDI_Reorder's shaping path. DrawText then renders the two UTF-16
code units separately. A valid pair needs shaping even without RTL text.
Keep isolated surrogates and the paragraph direction unchanged.

This does not add font fallback or full emoji sequence shaping. The selected
font must cover the supplementary character. GetTextExtentExPointW shares
this gate, so both ordinary measurement and output use the glyph cluster.

--- a/dlls/gdi32/text.c
+++ b/dlls/gdi32/text.c
@@ -409,7 +409,9 @@
     {
         if ((lpString[i] >= 0x900 && lpString[i] <= 0xfff) ||
             (lpString[i] >= 0x1cd0 && lpString[i] <= 0x1cff) ||
-            (lpString[i] >= 0xa840 && lpString[i] <= 0xa8ff))
+            (lpString[i] >= 0xa840 && lpString[i] <= 0xa8ff) ||
+            (lpString[i] >= 0xd800 && lpString[i] <= 0xdbff && i + 1 < uCount &&
+             lpString[i + 1] >= 0xdc00 && lpString[i + 1] <= 0xdfff))
             is_complex = TRUE;
     }
 
